{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791826375,"nonce":"GKmzauhMvNl5+jB1/JDovfkW3bU=","title":"Current ABI pin omits previously verified CSS order milestone","message":"Discovered while implementing input icons (Ashui 27e0124). Associated prior issues: Ashui 7977648 and shared ABI 62aa0b0. Cargo currently pins blinc_abi 4dc10a4 (idle equal-write suppression), which does not descend from the verified shared CSS order commit aca3248. The native HashLink Tree in that revision lacks the shared ordering implementation. Observed with a small search input: the leading part resolves data-side=leading and computed CSS order=-1, but stays after the text viewport (icon x=251,width=14; viewport x=9,width=242), matching the wrong dark snapshot. The same source has ordering only on the owned LayoutContext path. InputIcon now uses existing replaceChildren placement as RadioGroup does, so the feature does not require CSS order. Reconcile the idle revision with the previously verified order milestone, pin that combined revision, and rerun CssLayoutBindings order/paint/hit/focus tests before publishing the release. No native source was changed during the icon task.","files":null}]}